# LOCATION: .dockerignore   (NEW FILE, project root next to Dockerfile)
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and there was NO .dockerignore, so every file in the build folder went into the deployed image, including
# .env files and backups that hold live credentials. These entries keep secrets, version control data and junk out of the image.
# Nothing the application needs at run time is excluded (vendor/ is rebuilt inside the image by `composer install`; it is intentionally NOT listed here).
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.bak
*.zip
node_modules
storage/logs/*
npm-debug.log
.idea
.vscode
